        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "60708c99-e1f1-5af1-999d-64a061d98b13",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Columbia River, Oregon, Washington, Palm Beach County, Florida, Tanner Creek\n- Projects: Cascade Locks and Canal, Oregon Portage Railroad, Cascade Locks\n- People: Charles B. Moores\n- Roles: American businessman, politician\n\nFacts:\n- The Cascade Locks and Canal was a navigation project on the Columbia River between Oregon and Washington, and it was completed in 1896.\n- The Oregon Portage Railroad ran from Tanner Creek, near the future site of Bonneville Dam, to the Cascade Locks during the later years of the locks' construction.\n- Charles Bruce Moores was born on August 6, 1849, and was an American businessman and politician in Oregon.\n- Charles Bruce Moores died on January 5, 1930.\n- Lake Worth Lagoon is a lagoon in Palm Beach County, Florida.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
